====================================================================
THE J-SPACE NULL SURVIVES THE PENALTY SWEEP.
  jspace never clears the rank-matched control at any penalty in the
  grid, nor under nested CV (0.510 vs 0.580).
  Nested-CV ranking: orthogonal > random_subspace > residual > jspace.

  BUT RESTATE THE CLAIM. jspace moves from 0.513 at l2=1e-02 to
  0.513 at its best, so 'J-space is at chance' is too
  strong. The defensible claim is that J-space carries LESS role
  information than an arbitrary subspace of the same rank.

  ANOMALY EXPLAINED. At matched penalty l2=1e-02 residual (0.567)
  is level with or above random_subspace (0.580).
  'A projection beats its source' appears only at weak penalties,
  where the 5120-dim sources overfit and the 16-dim one does not.
  The fixed l2=1e-02 was in that regime. Report matched-penalty or
  nested-CV numbers; the fixed-penalty ranking was confounded.
